From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReplayMod-LegacyFabric <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:57:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Port ReplayMod to Fabric on 1.8.9 (Ornithe)

Make the 1.8.9-fabric target build and run on Ornithe, as used by
Polyfrost's OneClient. ReplayMod's <=1.12 code paths assume Forge, so each
use of Forge API gets an alternative which needs no loader API:

- Fabric entrypoint, settings, mod info and metadata instead of @Mod/FML
- render tick, RenderWorldLast, RenderHand, hotbar and crosshair events are
  fired from Mixins (they are Forge events on <=1.12)
- key bindings are registered once the game options exist, and the plugin
  channel and custom payload recording are handled by Mixins
- buttons injected into screens call their handler themselves; the OneClient
  main menu gets the button too
- scrolling in the replay adjusts the camera speed through a Mixin
- an access widener replaces the access transformers Forge applies
- Forge only compat code (FML handshake, coremod, mapwriter, ...) is stubbed
- a OneConfig entry with buttons for the viewer and the settings
- tools/OrnitheRetarget.java, run by the ornitheJar task, translates the
  jar from Legacy Fabric's names to Ornithe's

Shared code is changed with preprocessor conditions so the other targets
are unaffected.

